+      "logical_name": "p0104-fluctuation-question-source-scope",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "Source scope of the FPP fluctuation-exponent questions",
+      "statement": "For iid nearest-neighbor first-passage percolation on Z^d, Auffinger, Damron and Hanson Question 13 asks for a fluctuation exponent chi<1/2 in d>=2 under suitable conditions on the edge-weight law F, and chi=1/3 in d=2; Question 15 asks for chi>0 in suitable dimension. The questions do not specify the suitable laws. Their Section 3.1 also notes that the heuristic Var(T(0,x))~||x||^(2chi) has several possible rigorous meanings. A proof must fix the law class and exponent definition; these are posed questions, not established exponents.",
+      "proof_text": null,
+      "assumptions": ["Historical question as stated in the authors' survey", "No claim that current openness has been certified"],
+      "domain": "probability theory",
+      "source": {
+        "source_id": "arxiv:1511.03262:questions-13-15",
+        "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1511.03262",
+        "revision": "as-read-2026-10-10",
