+        "excerpt": null
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "key": "p0104-four-edge-mismatch",
+      "namespace": "probability.first-passage-percolation",
+      "logical_name": "four-edge-interface-matching-penalty-in-fpp",
+      "kind": "concept",
+      "title": "Four-edge matching penalty for scalar interface minima",
+      "statement": "In unrestricted iid edge FPP on Z^2 with weights uniform on {1,2}, let s=(0,0), t=(1,1), u=(1,0), v=(0,1), and set A1=w(s,u), A2=w(s,v), B1=w(u,t), B2=w(v,t). Then T(s,t)=min(A1+B1,A2+B2), whereas the scalar relaxation L=min(A1,A2)+min(B1,B2) can be smaller. The penalty G=T-L equals 1 on 2 of the 16 equally likely assignments and 0 otherwise. Exact values are Var(T)=23/64, Var(L)=3/8, Cov(L,G)=-1/16. Independence of the A and B edge sets does not remove the shared-interface matching constraint. This finite example does not imply an asymptotic fluctuation exponent.",
+      "proof_text": null,
+      "assumptions": ["Nearest-neighbor undirected FPP on the full Z^2 lattice", "Four independent displayed edges and all other edges also iid uniform on {1,2}", "w364 derived the example; w365 independently checked all 16 assignments with exact fractions"],
+      "domain": "probability theory",
+      "source": {
